.TH geectl-remote-add-containers 1  "geectl-remote-add-containers 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-add\-containers \- Add the maintained containers for a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the addition
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote add\-containers\fR [\fB\-\-extend\-package\-names\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add the maintained containers for a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the addition
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-extend\-package\-names\fR
Extend the package names with the container names
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package lives in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to add containers for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
